import "res://Visual Novel Romance/gd/Intro.gd" as snippets

~ start
do MusicManager.play_music_for("res://Visual Novel Romance/music/alarm-clock.mp3", 2.0)
do MusicManager.play_music("res://Visual Novel Romance/music/music1.ogg")
{{GameData.player_name}}: Ugh... here we go again. Another day at university
{{GameData.player_name}}: Felix, you came to sleep on top of me again
{{GameData.player_name}}: Well, how can I start the day?

- Have breakfast
    => breakfast

- Go back to sleep
    => sleep_more

~ breakfast

do SaveManager.set_checkpoint("breakfast")
do GameData.morning_route = "breakfast"
do SceneController.fade_to_black()
do SceneController.change_background("res://Visual Novel Romance/files/Blue.png")

You head to the kitchen to prepare your breakfast.

do SceneController.play_video("res://Visual Novel Romance/files/Breakfast_high.ogv")

{{GameData.player_name}}: Nothing could be better than this.

Felix sits on the table beside you, staring at your breakfast as if he hasn't eaten in days.

Despite his dramatic expression, he finished his own meal only a few minutes ago.

After breakfast, you finish getting ready and head to the university.

-- change image --

When you arrive, you meet your friend from the History department.

Gio: Hey, {{GameData.player_name}}. Do you remember my last study about local folklore? I found more information about the stories we used to hear when we were children.

You begin to remember the tales about dreams, where an Oneiric being protects the dreams of children and the world itself, keeping balance between them.

The legend says that when people stop dreaming, the Oneirics lose their strength, leaving humanity vulnerable to the attacks of their greatest nightmares.

Gio: Well, according to the book I'm reading, these stories are ancient and connected to rituals and ancestral temples.

Gio: This book suggests that, if those practices truly worked, people could reach a state where they were able to control their dreams. Dreams could even become a way to understand the present or glimpse the future.

Gio: I'm going to use this book for my research project. What did you think about it?

- Ask more about it
  => about

- Remember the childhood tales
  => tales

~ about
do SaveManager.set_checkpoint("about")

{{GameData.player_name}}: That's incredible. Is this book from the university? I'd love to hear more about your research.

Gio: Actually, I borrowed it from a small chapel not far from here. There are plenty of academic books on the subject, but I wanted firsthand accounts from people who actually lived through those experiences.

Gio: That's what makes this one so fascinating. It was written by a monk who documented his entire journey, from his first encounters with those practices to the day he became a monk himself.

The two of you continue talking until it's time for class.

Once inside the classroom, you struggle to stay awake. After managing to copy a few notes, the lecture finally comes to an end.

As everyone begins to leave, Gio catches up with you.

Gio: Heading home? Want to walk together?

You nod, and the two of you leave the university side by side.

=> work

~ tales
do SaveManager.set_checkpoint("tales")

{{GameData.player_name}}: So... the stories our parents used to tell us actually came from this folklore?

{{GameData.player_name}}: There were so many of them, but I can barely remember any now.

Gio: That's right. Over time, most people simply forgot them. Even so, many older generations still hold on to those legends.

Gio: We even have festivals and traditions that keep the stories alive, though they're nothing like they used to be.

{{GameData.player_name}}: I loved listening to those stories when I was a kid. But eventually everyone stopped talking about them.

{{GameData.player_name}}: I remember attending ceremonies where people encouraged us to treasure our dreams and never give up on them.

Gio: That's one of the core beliefs behind these traditions.

Gio: Dreams are said to reveal who we truly are... or, sometimes, the parts of ourselves we're trying to hide.

Gio: To stop dreaming, or to stop pursuing your goals, is like turning your back on your own identity.

{{GameData.player_name}}: That's... actually a really interesting way of looking at it.

{{GameData.player_name}}: I'd better get going. My class has probably already started.

Gio: See you around.

You make your way to class, though staying awake proves to be a challenge.

After scribbling down a few notes, the lecture finally ends.

As you're leaving campus, Gio catches up with you.

Gio: Ready to head home?

You agree, and the two of you walk away from the university together.

=> work


~ sleep_more
do SaveManager.set_checkpoint("sleep_more")
do GameData.morning_route = "sleep"
{{GameData.player_name}}: Just five more minutes.

do SceneController.sleep_sequence()
do MusicManager.play_music("res://Visual Novel Romance/music/music1.ogg")
Some time later...

{{GameData.player_name}}: Wait... What time is it?!

You hurriedly grab the first clothes you can find, only to notice they're covered in Felix's fur. With no time to waste, you throw on a darker outfit to hide it as best as you can.

You rush out of the house and make your way to the university, already running late.

By the time you arrive, class has already begun. You quietly take your seat and start taking notes.

After class, you run into Mary.

Mary: Hey. How have you been?

- Not so well
  => not_well

- I've been doing alright.
  => good

~ not_well
do SaveManager.set_checkpoint("not_well")
{{GameData.player_name}}: I didn't sleep very well. I accidentally fell back asleep this morning and ended up running late... But enough about me. How have you been?

Mary: I've been really busy lately, but I'm doing well.

{{GameData.player_name}}: I'm glad to hear that. I know how it is. Between classes, research, and assignments, there's always something to do.

=> work

~ good

do SaveManager.set_checkpoint("good")

{{GameData.player_name}}: I've been doing alright, all things considered. You're heading home through Main Avenue, right?

Mary: Yeah. We can walk together if you'd like.

=> work

~ work

The two of you leave campus together, chatting about extracurricular credits, hobbies, and upcoming assignments.

Eventually, you say goodbye and enter a nearby office building.

It's your workplace.

You settle into your desk and spend the next few hours working, occasionally chatting with your coworkers.

After hours of typing, you decide you need a short break, even though it's not lunchtime yet.

- Hide in the restroom and check your phone.
  => restroom

- Grab a cup of coffee.
  => coffee

- Take a quick nap.
  => nap

- Pretend to be working.
  => pretend

~ restroom
do SaveManager.set_checkpoint("restroom")
You spend about fifteen minutes in the restroom scrolling through your phone.

- Message a friend.
  => message

- Keep scrolling through social media.
  => feed

~ message
do SaveManager.set_checkpoint("message")
if GameData.morning_route == "breakfast":

	do GameData.last_person_texted = "gio"
	You decide to send Gio a quick message.

	=> after_message

elif GameData.morning_route == "sleep":

	do GameData.last_person_texted = "mary"
	You decide to send Mary a quick message.

	=> after_message

~ after_message
do SaveManager.set_checkpoint("after_message")
You wait for a reply.

Nothing.

With a quiet sigh, you put your phone away and return to work. Before long, your shift comes to an end.

=> go_home

=> END

~ feed
do SaveManager.set_checkpoint("feed")
You keep scrolling longer than you intended.

By the time you put your phone away, you feel even more exhausted than before.

You finish your shift almost on autopilot, and before you realize it, you're already standing at your front door.

=> go_home

=> END

~ coffee
do SaveManager.set_checkpoint("coffe")

%70
	do GameData.change_health(-5)
	The coffee is much hotter than expected, and you burn your tongue.

Feeling a little more awake, you return to work and finish the rest of your shift.

=> go_home

%30
	The coffee tastes surprisingly bitter.

Feeling a little more awake, you return to work and finish the rest of your shift.

=> go_home

%50
	It's actually a really good cup of coffee.

Feeling a little more awake, you return to work and finish the rest of your shift.

=> go_home

=> END

~ nap
do SaveManager.set_checkpoint("nap")
You close your eyes for what feels like only a minute.

When you wake up, a coworker is already complaining that you've been asleep.

You brush it off, finish your work, and head home after your shift.

=> go_home

=> END

~ pretend
do SaveManager.set_checkpoint("pretend")
Luckily, you'd already finished most of your work.

The rest of the afternoon is spent looking busy whenever someone walks by.

You even realize you could pretend to finish the same project tomorrow.

Once your shift ends, you head home.

=> go_home

~ go_home
do SaveManager.set_checkpoint("go_home")
do SceneController.fade_to_black()
-- Home animation

=> END

=> END

=> END

=> END

~ END